      "subject_newsroom_count": 3,
      "summary": "The University Hospital Center (CHU) in Pointe-à-Pitre, Guadeloupe was the target of a major cyberattack that disrupted computer systems and forced staff to revert to paper records and manual processes. The hospital declared its emergency plan (plan blanc), suspended some scheduled activities and consultations, and said investigations and recovery efforts were underway while authorities and technical teams worked to restore services."
