      "subject_newsroom_count": 12,
      "summary": "Multiple French outlets report that President Emmanuel Macron has publicly said he is exploring the idea of enshrining a so‑called 'règle d’or' (golden rule) budget constraint in the Constitution, potentially requiring a special parliamentary procedure or Congress to adopt it; the proposal echoes a 2011 draft linked to Nicolas Sarkozy, has drawn approval from right and far‑right parties, and is being examined alongside legal, technical and political safeguards described in the press."
